								<p style="text-align:justify;color:white; padding-bottom:100px">The price an advertisement receives for 1000 exposures of an online advertisement is known as the CPM, or Cost Per Mille, rate. CPM merely estimates the cost of having the advertisement aired; it does not track any actions that consumers make. Several performance marketers are placing a greater emphasis on KPIs with a tangible, initiative significance rather than CPM.</p>
